<title>Syria: the situation</title>
<link>https://map.igred.org/crisis/syria/</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">igred-summary-syria-2026-11-10T18:01:23.604Z</guid>
<pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:01:23 GMT</pubDate>
<description>&lt;p&gt;Syria has begun dispatching troops to Saudi Arabia to fight the Houthis, while denying any deployment inside Yemen. Saudi-led forces and Yemen's Iran-backed Houthis have escalated attacks, including a strike that damaged the Saudi Aramco Tower in Riyadh. In Damascus countryside, heavy clashes erupted around Wadi Barada between Syrian forces and unidentified opponents. Jordan and Syria have signed eleven cooperation agreements covering economic projects, security coordination and a rail link, deepening bilateral ties. The conflict caused 2,732 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/11/10/attacks-escalate-between-saudi-led-forces-and-yemens-iran-backed-houthis?traffic_source=rss&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/10/world/middleeast/syria-weighs-sending-troops-to-aid-saudi-war-with-houthis.html&quot;&gt;The New York Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMixwFBVV95cUxNdkdRX3ZKb0hFX0EtM25yamlZYWJ3dVh4UlZJelZWMmpSOVlSR3dzdVg1TEFoNmJoZFM4Q2dDeUtkQ1RCYWs1cFNsRlctRl9XeEF2VzM0N29BRzBMMlVhUVBEQmdHV0hwand0N0xGQ2JKZE0tR0NYaS1yRzBqN1JxcDg1ckxhRm96SThIeGVYcUlOY1ZLWVl3UG9senBxOGtOdk11TlMwT2haVEdoa1hvYXIwZjhZZXJCZkVmYUtfay1oS3lnOFJR?oc=5&quot;&gt;Reuters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/07/world/middleeast/more-than-50-killed-in-yemen.html&quot;&gt;The New York Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/08/world/middleeast/saudi-aramco-tower-riyadh-hit.html&quot;&gt;The New York Times&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
